WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:10.231
Eight-ball pool, on a full-size table with real ball physics. Two players, or four if you want to play in teams. And the computer can take a seat.

2
00:00:10.931 --> 00:00:23.254
Drag anywhere on the table to aim. The dotted line shows where the cue ball goes. The yellow line shows where the ball you hit will travel, and a short line shows where the cue ball goes afterwards.

3
00:00:23.404 --> 00:00:26.276
Use the slider to set the power, and press shoot.

4
00:00:26.977 --> 00:00:36.067
The little cue ball lets you choose where you strike it. Hit the top for follow, the bottom to draw the ball back, and the sides to put spin on the shot.

5
00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:41.141
Spin really does change how the balls bounce and roll, so it's worth practising.

6
00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:48.062
After you sink your first ball, you own either the solids or the stripes. Keep shooting while you pot your own.

7
00:00:48.212 --> 00:00:56.956
Miss everything, scratch, or hit the wrong ball first, and it's a foul. Your opponent gets ball in hand, and can place the cue ball anywhere.

8
00:00:57.656 --> 00:01:02.713
Clear all your balls, and then sink the eight to win. Sink it early, and you lose.
